WEBVTT

00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:05.930
bokura nara daijoubu

00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:05.930
Because we’re still doing okay,

00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:12.390
mada tsuyoku nareru kara

00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:12.390
we can become even stronger!

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:17.900
takaihiroi sora megake

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:17.900
Aiming for the tall and wide sky,

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:21.450
kinou made no boku wo hanatsu

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:21.450
I let go of what I was up until yesterday.

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:24.260
miesuita uso mo, taikutsu na

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:24.260
Those lies that were easily seen through and my tedious day-by-day life;

00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:26.980
hibi mo, zenbu hodoite

00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:26.980
I left them both behind.

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:29.870
atarashii asa ni me wo hosome

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:29.870
I narrowed my eyes at the new morning

00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:33.280
kyou mo bokutachi wa ikiteku

00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:33.280
Today we shall also venture out
to live our lives again.

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:36.720
sukoshi nami utsu sabishisadatte

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:36.720
Even the slight loneliness that sometimes comes about,

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:39.460
taisetsu ni omoeteru

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:39.460
I consider important.

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:45.070
itsuka kanjita shinjitsu mo

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:45.070
Even the truth I felt some day…

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:51.440
massugu koko kara asu ni mukatteru

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:51.440
…is urging us to go on into the future.

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:56.450
bokutachi ga mezashita sekai

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:56.450
The world that we had all aimed for…

00:00:56.450 --> 00:01:03.470
donna kakomo kakaeta mama kitto tadoritsuku

00:00:56.450 --> 00:01:03.470
We will arrive at it, no matter what our pasts are.

00:01:03.470 --> 00:01:08.460
fumidashita kewashii michi mo

00:01:03.470 --> 00:01:08.460
We continued forward, even if it is a steep path…

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:11.900
bokura nara daijoubu,

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:11.900
…because we’re still doing okay,

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:18.280
mada tsuyoku nareru kara

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:18.280
and we can become even stronger!

00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:45.750
Up until recently,
I didn’t really think that…

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:52.960
…I’d end up living again in the town…

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:55.960
…that I lived in when Mom was still alive.

00:02:15.110 --> 00:02:16.110
Oh my…

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:18.820
Were the stores right in front of the station that tiny?

00:02:19.610 --> 00:02:21.120
But even so, it’s nostalgic.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:25.960
Let’s see… It’s this way.

00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:33.760
I thought this street was
wider than this, too.

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:36.760
I guess it’s because I’ve grown up now.

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:40.050
Some things have changed while others have not.

00:02:41.630 --> 00:02:42.550
Oh!

00:02:43.170 --> 00:02:44.770
The Fukubuku Department Store!

00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:47.060
So it was that small?

00:02:48.260 --> 00:02:50.730
Mother would always take me there.

00:02:51.770 --> 00:02:57.490
I was always eating ice cream on the roof with the two girls next door.

00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:01.820
Those twins, Kaoruko-chan and Sumireko-chan…

00:03:01.820 --> 00:03:03.880
…they were so cute.

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:10.710
Nozomu-chan! Nozomu-chan!

00:03:10.710 --> 00:03:15.920
I want to be your bride when I grow up!

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:17.220
Me too!

00:03:17.220 --> 00:03:20.140
I want to be your bride!

00:03:20.140 --> 00:03:22.810
Eh? Really?

00:03:23.670 --> 00:03:25.430
But… what should I do?

00:03:25.430 --> 00:03:27.180
There’s only one of me!

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:31.110
That’s okay! We’ll both be your brides!

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:35.440
Of course! We’ll be your wives together!

00:03:36.110 --> 00:03:37.780
Promise?

00:03:38.270 --> 00:03:40.570
Uh… okay. I promise.

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:51.160
Thinking about it now,
I can’t believe what I did back then.

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:52.380
It’s so memorable…

00:03:53.330 --> 00:03:54.340
Ah, I’m sorry!

00:03:56.790 --> 00:03:57.790
It’s a statue.

00:03:57.790 --> 00:03:58.920
Oh, that kid…

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:00.460
How embarrassing.

00:04:05.590 --> 00:04:09.480
I wonder if Kaoruko-chan and Sumireko-chan still live in this town?

00:04:10.470 --> 00:04:12.610
Perhaps we’ll have an emotional reunion or something?

00:04:18.230 --> 00:04:21.900
Are you ready for this, Misses?

00:04:22.270 --> 00:04:23.110
Yes.

00:04:23.110 --> 00:04:25.360
It will be alright, Kenmochi-san.

00:04:25.900 --> 00:04:29.360
When girls from the Sakurazuki family reach the age of fifteen,

00:04:29.360 --> 00:04:32.950
they must go experience
a normal life.

00:04:32.950 --> 00:04:37.380
Papa said that this is the rule of the Sakurazuki family.

00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:40.960
Yes, Kira-sama, Yura-sama.

00:04:54.220 --> 00:04:56.470
It’s about to begin, Yura-chan.

00:04:56.470 --> 00:04:57.980
Good luck, Kira-chan.

00:04:57.980 --> 00:05:00.070
Please take your purse.

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:02.480
Thank you, Kenmochi-san.

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:06.280
It’s the first time we’re carrying a purse. I’m so excited!

00:05:06.650 --> 00:05:09.250
The first order that Papa had given us:

00:05:09.250 --> 00:05:12.200
We must begin by shopping at a convenience store.

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:13.870
Let’s go, Yura-chan.

00:05:13.870 --> 00:05:15.790
Yes, Kira-chan.

00:05:24.380 --> 00:05:25.630
Umm…

00:05:25.630 --> 00:05:28.010
“Pass the front of a convenience store, and…”

00:05:31.550 --> 00:05:33.480
Wow! What an incredibly high-class car!

00:05:36.390 --> 00:05:38.100
Twin girls?

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:40.520
Maybe they’re Kaoruko-chan and Sumireko-chan?!

00:05:41.480 --> 00:05:44.440
Ah! Isn’t it Nozomu-chan?

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:47.610
And we meet each other here, no less!

00:05:47.610 --> 00:05:49.410
It must be destiny, right?

00:05:49.780 --> 00:05:51.250
Oh, it can’t be…

00:05:52.860 --> 00:05:55.870
Mom, that older boy seems strange.

00:05:55.870 --> 00:05:58.290
I think he must be playing the Laughing Game.

00:05:55.870 --> 00:06:00.000
[Note: A reference to drunkenness or eroticism in the Edo period.]

00:06:04.750 --> 00:06:06.970
But still, it really might be them.

00:06:07.420 --> 00:06:08.550
Let’s find out.

00:06:09.880 --> 00:06:12.510
Foie gras-flavored potato chips, check.

00:06:12.510 --> 00:06:15.720
Super deluxe roast beef onigiri, check.

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:19.900
Gran Marnier Fumi yogurt, check!
Caviar cup noodles, check!

00:06:20.850 --> 00:06:22.480
Okay! That should be enough to stock the kitchen!

00:06:22.480 --> 00:06:24.280
Do you agree, Yura-chan?

00:06:24.280 --> 00:06:26.900
Really, Kira-chan!

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:29.570
It isn’t them.

00:06:29.570 --> 00:06:33.160
They’re a little strange, but they are cute.

00:06:33.740 --> 00:06:35.870
Now, we just need to go pay for this.

00:06:35.870 --> 00:06:36.480
Yeah.

00:06:37.700 --> 00:06:41.410
Yura-chan, I think the guy over there is staring at us.

00:06:41.410 --> 00:06:44.000
Really! What is he doing?

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:46.230
Maybe he’s a scary person!

00:06:46.230 --> 00:06:46.760
Eh?

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:49.360
Kenmochi told us,

00:06:49.360 --> 00:06:53.590
“You’ll encounter scary people from time to time in this world, so please be careful!”

00:06:53.590 --> 00:06:55.230
Eh? What do we do?

00:06:58.220 --> 00:06:59.600
We’d better run!

00:07:02.060 --> 00:07:03.770
Huh? Your purse!

00:07:06.520 --> 00:07:09.520
It’s the first time I’ve seen such a scary person in the flesh.

00:07:09.520 --> 00:07:10.530
Yeah, you’re right.

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:11.700
Umm… here.

00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:19.630
Hey, wait!

00:07:20.160 --> 00:07:21.830
This person is scary!

00:07:21.830 --> 00:07:23.420
Huh? No way!

00:07:23.960 --> 00:07:25.170
You! Hold it right there!

00:07:25.170 --> 00:07:26.960
You’re mistaken!

00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:29.220
Wait right there!

00:07:33.010 --> 00:07:35.930
If you want to pick on my mistresses, go eat shit.

00:07:35.930 --> 00:07:36.760
Kenmochi-san…

00:07:36.760 --> 00:07:37.300
I’m scared!

00:07:37.300 --> 00:07:39.680
Misses, are you harmed?

00:07:39.680 --> 00:07:41.180
Oww.

00:07:41.180 --> 00:07:43.400
Hey, let’s have a little talk
in the backroom.

00:07:44.940 --> 00:07:46.440
This is a misunderstanding!

00:07:46.850 --> 00:07:48.860
I was just going to return
that girl’s purse…

00:07:49.770 --> 00:07:50.940
Hey!

00:07:50.940 --> 00:07:51.910
Sorry to bother you!

00:07:51.910 --> 00:07:53.660
Wait up!

00:07:51.910 --> 00:07:53.660
Our purse…

00:07:54.070 --> 00:07:56.530
It’s not here! Did we lose it?

00:07:56.530 --> 00:07:58.370
Did it get stolen?

00:07:58.910 --> 00:08:03.090
Miss, the Laughing Boy picked it up.

00:08:04.830 --> 00:08:05.960
Is that true?

00:08:05.960 --> 00:08:07.380
Yeah! I saw it!

00:08:07.380 --> 00:08:08.880
That can’t be!

00:08:12.880 --> 00:08:14.850
What was it with them?

00:08:15.510 --> 00:08:16.930
But they were really cute…

00:08:30.440 --> 00:08:31.740
Sourin Temple.

00:08:32.480 --> 00:08:37.780
Here it is. Let’s see… go around to the back yard.

00:08:43.740 --> 00:08:45.590
Hello!?

00:08:47.660 --> 00:08:48.750
Maybe they’re not in?

00:08:49.670 --> 00:08:51.170
If only the shutter were open.

00:08:52.170 --> 00:08:54.510
I did get on an earlier train
than expected…

00:08:57.160 --> 00:09:00.430
I guess I’ll be living here for the next two years.

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:02.940
Graves.

00:09:03.930 --> 00:09:05.440
They’re kinda creepy.

00:09:19.450 --> 00:09:22.750
Ah! Someone’s trying to deface the shrine of the twins!

00:09:26.020 --> 00:09:27.830
You can’t do that!

00:09:27.830 --> 00:09:29.380
More twins?

00:09:30.830 --> 00:09:35.140
Oh my, Nozomu-kun, you’re finally here and you’ve grown quite a bit.

00:09:35.630 --> 00:09:37.170
Is that Nozomu-oniichan?

00:09:37.170 --> 00:09:37.890
Yes.

00:09:39.260 --> 00:09:40.850
Hello, I’m Nozomu.

00:09:40.850 --> 00:09:43.190
Ahhh! Welcome!

00:09:44.800 --> 00:09:45.140
Umm…

00:09:45.640 --> 00:09:47.890
I’m Hinagiku Ruru!

00:09:47.890 --> 00:09:49.520
I’m Hinagiku Rara!

00:09:52.270 --> 00:09:53.690
We’re pleased to meet you!

00:09:53.690 --> 00:09:57.580
Uh, t-thanks… Pleased to meet you.

00:10:00.360 --> 00:10:01.200
Umm…

00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:03.320
What is it?

00:10:03.320 --> 00:10:06.280
Thank you for taking me in for the next two years, Miyabi-obasan.

00:10:06.280 --> 00:10:08.290
I refuse to be called “obasan.”

00:10:08.290 --> 00:10:09.670
Call me Miyabi-san.

00:10:09.670 --> 00:10:11.420
Okay…

00:10:11.920 --> 00:10:15.610
Nozomu-kun, your presence
will help us a lot.

00:10:15.610 --> 00:10:19.010
Our family takes care of this temple year-round.

00:10:19.010 --> 00:10:24.340
From now on, you’ll be the pillar of support for the three of us!

00:10:24.340 --> 00:10:26.770
You can be our bodyguard and servant!

00:10:27.350 --> 00:10:29.570
You sure are using some difficult words.

00:10:29.570 --> 00:10:33.810
But, your father’s transfer really did come quite suddenly.

00:10:33.810 --> 00:10:36.900
On top of that, for it to be two years in an astronomical observatory in Hawaii…

00:10:37.440 --> 00:10:41.950
Dad told me that I can decide where I want to live.

00:10:44.200 --> 00:10:45.790
Nozomu, what do you plan to do?

00:10:47.660 --> 00:10:49.410
The decision is entirely yours.

00:10:49.410 --> 00:10:51.630
You also have your high school entrance exams to worry about, so…

00:10:52.160 --> 00:10:55.080
…do you want to come with me or do you want to remain in Japan?

00:10:55.080 --> 00:10:58.420
Sorry. No matter what, you have to change schools.

00:11:02.550 --> 00:11:06.890
And so, you’ve decided that high school entrance exams were more important.

00:11:06.890 --> 00:11:09.190
It’s not like that…

00:11:09.640 --> 00:11:14.860
Dad had said that he wanted to try working at that astronomical observatory for a while.

00:11:15.980 --> 00:11:18.210
I know Dad has been making sacrifices in his work

00:11:18.210 --> 00:11:22.830
ever since Mom died,
so he could raise me.

00:11:23.240 --> 00:11:27.170
It’s a rare chance, so I thought I’d let him concentrate on his work for once.

00:11:27.660 --> 00:11:29.990
That’s great! What a good kid.

00:11:29.990 --> 00:11:33.580
If I were a middle school student,
I would fall in love with you!

00:11:33.580 --> 00:11:34.000
Eh?

00:11:34.410 --> 00:11:35.960
No, Mom!

00:11:35.960 --> 00:11:39.130
It’s already been decided that Onii-chan will be my groom!

00:11:39.130 --> 00:11:41.510
Me too! He’s going to be my groom too!

00:11:42.300 --> 00:11:43.300
Onii-chan!

00:11:43.300 --> 00:11:44.350
Don’t stray!

00:11:44.350 --> 00:11:47.510
Stray? Hey, that’s going a bit far…

00:11:47.510 --> 00:11:49.350
Hello, Miyabi-san!

00:11:49.930 --> 00:11:51.020
Ah!

00:11:52.720 --> 00:11:55.320
Welcome, Kaoruko-chan, Sumireko-chan.

00:11:55.940 --> 00:11:57.400
Welcome!

00:11:59.270 --> 00:12:01.780
Kaoruko-chan. Sumireko-chan.

00:12:02.150 --> 00:12:03.490
Nozomu-chan.

00:12:03.490 --> 00:12:04.780
We really wanted to see you!

00:12:11.330 --> 00:12:13.840
Kaoruko-chan. Sumireko-chan.

00:12:14.290 --> 00:12:15.560
Nozomu-chan.

00:12:15.560 --> 00:12:16.630
We really wanted to see you!

00:12:18.750 --> 00:12:21.590
Okay, you two, come on in.

00:12:21.590 --> 00:12:22.800
Okay!

00:12:25.720 --> 00:12:27.140
Long time no see.

00:12:27.140 --> 00:12:29.840
Really! It’s so nostalgic.

00:12:29.840 --> 00:12:32.390
We haven’t seen you since kindergarten!

00:12:33.850 --> 00:12:37.650
Oh my goodness, they have become many times cuter now they’ve grown up!

00:12:44.780 --> 00:12:47.160
The Ichijou family are supporters of the temple.

00:12:47.650 --> 00:12:49.120
Is that so?

00:12:49.700 --> 00:12:54.120
They were really looking forward to it when I told the two of them that you were coming!

00:12:54.870 --> 00:12:55.710
Yeah!

00:12:55.710 --> 00:13:00.080
I wonder if that “looking forward” there has any special connotations…

00:13:00.080 --> 00:13:01.130
No, impossible.

00:13:01.130 --> 00:13:04.390
But they did come out of their way to come meet me.

00:13:05.210 --> 00:13:06.720
Nozomu-chan, do you remember?

00:13:07.720 --> 00:13:10.100
The time when we were little,
on the roof of the department store…

00:13:11.520 --> 00:13:12.850
It’s a promise!

00:13:13.300 --> 00:13:15.310
We ate ice cream very often, didn’t we?

00:13:15.310 --> 00:13:17.060
We sure did!

00:13:18.310 --> 00:13:19.990
I guess so.

00:13:20.810 --> 00:13:23.910
So, I guess we’ll be
in the same school again?

00:13:24.360 --> 00:13:25.230
Yeah!

00:13:25.230 --> 00:13:27.290
It’d be nice if we could end up in the same class, eh?

00:13:28.610 --> 00:13:31.530
No fair, you two!

00:13:31.530 --> 00:13:35.130
We end up in different classes because we’re too young!

00:13:36.080 --> 00:13:37.650
That’s it!

00:13:37.650 --> 00:13:39.000
Onii-chan, come on!

00:13:39.000 --> 00:13:40.670
I’m going to introduce you to Billy.

00:13:41.370 --> 00:13:42.380
Billy?

00:13:51.630 --> 00:13:52.940
Ah, it’s a goat!

00:13:54.080 --> 00:13:55.140
It’s cute!

00:13:55.140 --> 00:13:56.730
He’s bigger than he was before, right?

00:13:56.730 --> 00:13:57.890
Yeah!

00:13:57.890 --> 00:14:00.280
He can sit now.

00:14:02.150 --> 00:14:04.230
Eh, it’s cute.

00:14:04.690 --> 00:14:07.240
Onii-chan, why don’t you hold him?

00:14:13.530 --> 00:14:14.710
Incredible!

00:14:14.710 --> 00:14:18.240
He’s holding it for the first time,
and it’s getting along with him!

00:14:18.240 --> 00:14:20.210
I don’t think we’re getting along…

00:14:20.210 --> 00:14:22.130
You little…

00:14:22.130 --> 00:14:24.170
That’s our Nozomu-chan!

00:14:24.170 --> 00:14:27.880
You were so good with animals back then, weren’t you?

00:14:27.880 --> 00:14:30.470
You’re so nice and so popular.

00:14:30.470 --> 00:14:33.220
I’m so happy that you’re still so nice.

00:14:33.220 --> 00:14:34.850
Yeah. I’m VERY happy.

00:14:40.560 --> 00:14:42.390
I’m glad, Billy.

00:14:42.390 --> 00:14:45.360
You can play with Onii-chan every day!

00:14:47.400 --> 00:14:48.620
Every day?

00:14:49.110 --> 00:14:50.620
Will I be okay?

00:14:57.450 --> 00:14:59.240
What are you looking at?

00:14:59.240 --> 00:15:00.500
What, what?

00:15:00.500 --> 00:15:03.170
Do you know anything about the grave of the twins?

00:15:03.170 --> 00:15:04.750
Yeah, we know.

00:15:04.750 --> 00:15:08.460
Yeah, the shrine has a sad love legend.

00:15:08.460 --> 00:15:09.510
A legend?

00:15:09.960 --> 00:15:14.850
A long time ago, a set of twins both fell in love with the same man.

00:15:14.850 --> 00:15:18.220
They shared the same feelings and the same love.

00:15:18.220 --> 00:15:20.600
The young man could not decide between his feelings for the two girls, so…

00:15:20.600 --> 00:15:23.150
…they were pained, saddened, and didn’t know what to do.

00:15:23.390 --> 00:15:27.530
The twins became small birds and flew off into the sky.

00:15:28.820 --> 00:15:32.740
Yes, I know about this story!

00:15:32.740 --> 00:15:33.570
Me too! Me too!

00:15:34.280 --> 00:15:36.490
I see. So this legend is…

00:15:36.490 --> 00:15:40.450
Oh no, Nozomu-chan. It’s just a legend.

00:15:40.450 --> 00:15:41.240
But you know…

00:15:41.240 --> 00:15:46.130
They say that a lot of twins are born in this town because the grave of the twins is here.

00:15:46.670 --> 00:15:48.250
Now that you mention it…

00:15:48.250 --> 00:15:48.840
Aren’t there?

00:15:49.510 --> 00:15:51.380
It is true!

00:15:51.380 --> 00:15:53.390
I’ve seen three sets of twins
in just one day!

00:15:55.380 --> 00:15:56.930
We’re leaving!

00:15:56.930 --> 00:15:58.550
We’ll see you tomorrow, Nozomu-chan!

00:15:58.550 --> 00:16:00.600
I’ll see you at school!

00:16:00.600 --> 00:16:03.230
Bye bye! See you later!

00:16:07.150 --> 00:16:08.940
This way! This way!

00:16:10.380 --> 00:16:11.450
Come on in!

00:16:12.880 --> 00:16:14.900
This is Nozomu-niichan’s…

00:16:14.900 --> 00:16:16.200
…room!

00:16:23.410 --> 00:16:24.910
Hey, Onii-chan!

00:16:24.910 --> 00:16:26.660
What is this box?

00:16:26.660 --> 00:16:28.710
It seems really sturdy.

00:16:28.710 --> 00:16:30.380
What’s in it?

00:16:30.380 --> 00:16:31.470
Something good.

00:16:34.590 --> 00:16:36.470
Wow!

00:16:36.470 --> 00:16:39.930
It’s a telescope!
Can we use it right now?

00:16:39.930 --> 00:16:43.060
It’ll take me some time to set up.
Maybe next Sunday?

00:16:43.060 --> 00:16:45.730
Hey, what is this?

00:16:45.730 --> 00:16:46.680
It’s an eyepiece.

00:16:46.680 --> 00:16:47.730
And this?

00:16:47.730 --> 00:16:48.810
It’s a star diagonal.

00:16:48.810 --> 00:16:50.150
How about this?

00:16:50.150 --> 00:16:50.980
It’s a secondary lens.

00:16:50.980 --> 00:16:52.400
And this? This?

00:16:52.400 --> 00:16:53.110
It’s a tripod.

00:16:53.110 --> 00:16:54.940
What is this? It looks strange…

00:16:54.940 --> 00:16:56.570
It is weird!

00:16:56.570 --> 00:16:59.660
It’s more weird–

00:17:02.030 --> 00:17:03.330
It seems like…

00:17:03.330 --> 00:17:06.170
…my first day in this town is about to end.

00:17:08.460 --> 00:17:11.710
Miyabi-san, I’m going to go look at the stars in a bit. Is that okay with you?

00:17:11.710 --> 00:17:13.850
You can get to the roof
from the second floor.

00:17:14.340 --> 00:17:15.840
Be careful not to fall off.

00:17:16.380 --> 00:17:17.550
Okay.

00:17:18.010 --> 00:17:18.760
I want to go!

00:17:18.760 --> 00:17:19.510
Me too!

00:17:19.970 --> 00:17:22.390
It’s bathtime for you two.

00:17:22.390 --> 00:17:23.730
Phooey.

00:17:29.770 --> 00:17:33.160
Wow, there are so many stars!

00:17:33.570 --> 00:17:35.370
They’re much better here
than in Tokyo!

00:17:36.480 --> 00:17:38.210
The star Regulus,
in the constellation of Leo.

00:17:40.860 --> 00:17:42.720
The star Spica,
in the constellation of Virgo.

00:17:44.450 --> 00:17:46.210
The star Arcturus,
in the constellation of Libra.

00:17:48.660 --> 00:17:49.840
The Big Dipper.

00:17:50.870 --> 00:17:54.340
And the star Polaris,
in the constellation of Ursa Minor.

00:17:57.260 --> 00:18:00.180
No! I want to see Mom!

00:18:00.800 --> 00:18:03.390
Hey Nozomu, look over there.

00:18:03.390 --> 00:18:05.190
Your mom is at that star.

00:18:06.350 --> 00:18:10.250
That star will always be
looking out for you.

00:18:10.250 --> 00:18:11.360
Really?

00:18:11.360 --> 00:18:15.570
Yeah. And when you cry, your mother will be smiling through the stars.

00:18:16.980 --> 00:18:18.700
Dad was really clever…

00:18:19.190 --> 00:18:22.830
Polaris can be seen all year,
and that’s why he said that.

00:18:24.030 --> 00:18:27.000
Goodnight, Dad, Mom…

00:18:28.540 --> 00:18:30.960
Okay! Ruru, Rara, let’s hurry!

00:18:30.960 --> 00:18:31.880
You too, Nozomu-kun.

00:18:33.710 --> 00:18:35.760
Here’s your lunch.

00:18:36.170 --> 00:18:37.090
Sorry to inconvenience you.

00:18:37.090 --> 00:18:39.220
Are you sure you don’t need me to come along?

00:18:39.760 --> 00:18:43.220
I’m fine. I’m sure I’ll be okay.

00:18:43.220 --> 00:18:44.970
Hey, Onii-chan…

00:18:44.970 --> 00:18:46.740
Let’s go part of the way together!

00:18:48.430 --> 00:18:49.650
Okay, I’m off!

00:18:50.230 --> 00:18:51.570
Be careful!

00:18:55.020 --> 00:18:56.310
I’m changing schools.

00:18:56.310 --> 00:18:59.740
Maybe I’ll be in the same class with Kaoruko-chan and Sumireko-chan!

00:19:03.510 --> 00:19:06.700
This school is so big and so beautiful.

00:19:07.180 --> 00:19:08.840
I wonder if I’ll see people I knew in kindergarten

00:19:08.840 --> 00:19:10.960
other than Kaoruko-chan
and Sumireko-chan.

00:19:15.690 --> 00:19:17.840
Oh! Is that you, Keisuke?!

00:19:18.420 --> 00:19:20.300
Nozomu, it’s definitely you!

00:19:21.210 --> 00:19:22.560
Yay!

00:19:23.260 --> 00:19:25.390
It’s been a while, Keisuke!

00:19:25.390 --> 00:19:29.640
Now that you’re back,
we can have some fun!

00:19:29.640 --> 00:19:32.100
We can play toy models again!

00:19:32.100 --> 00:19:33.180
Yeah!

00:19:33.180 --> 00:19:35.100
So, let’s go play together again.

00:19:35.100 --> 00:19:38.990
Umm… but I don’t think I have any interest in toy models.

00:19:39.400 --> 00:19:41.700
It’s not what you think.

00:19:42.150 --> 00:19:44.070
You sure haven’t changed.

00:19:44.070 --> 00:19:44.830
Sorry about that.

00:19:46.140 --> 00:19:48.120
It would be good if we were
in the same class.

00:19:48.120 --> 00:19:48.830
Yeah.

00:19:50.740 --> 00:19:53.370
So you’re the transfer student,
Futami Nozomu-kun, right?

00:19:53.370 --> 00:19:54.290
Yes.

00:19:54.290 --> 00:19:58.710
I’m the teacher in charge of class 3-1, Momoi Ai.

00:19:59.040 --> 00:20:02.680
They have such pretty teachers here in this city.

00:20:03.340 --> 00:20:05.970
Good morning, Momoi-sensei.

00:20:05.970 --> 00:20:08.060
Ah, the Ichijou sisters are here.
Good morning.

00:20:08.800 --> 00:20:10.480
Morning, Nozomu-chan!

00:20:10.930 --> 00:20:12.100
M-Morning!

00:20:13.100 --> 00:20:17.150
It’s too bad, you’ll be
in Momoi-sensei’s class.

00:20:17.150 --> 00:20:19.690
I see, we’ll be in different classes then.

00:20:19.690 --> 00:20:21.570
However, you’re in the class next to ours!

00:20:21.570 --> 00:20:22.820
We’ll see each other a lot!

00:20:23.320 --> 00:20:26.330
That’s because my class is the only one
that’s short of students.

00:20:26.970 --> 00:20:30.330
Futami-kun, you’re not the only transfer student today.

00:20:30.330 --> 00:20:31.790
There’s more?

00:20:31.790 --> 00:20:33.620
We’re very sorry!

00:20:33.620 --> 00:20:35.130
Sorry for being late!

00:20:35.830 --> 00:20:36.880
Those voices…

00:20:39.420 --> 00:20:40.590
You’re the ones from yesterday…?

00:20:42.670 --> 00:20:43.430
You know them?

00:20:44.130 --> 00:20:46.090
Ah, that was a misunderstanding!

00:20:46.090 --> 00:20:48.180
I just picked up your purse, and…

00:20:48.180 --> 00:20:49.810
It wasn’t anything strange–

00:20:49.180 --> 00:20:50.520
We’re sorry!

00:20:51.600 --> 00:20:55.180
You were kind to us and
we mistreated you.

00:20:55.180 --> 00:20:56.520
We’re really really sorry!

00:20:57.060 --> 00:20:58.480
Umm…

00:20:59.060 --> 00:21:04.980
We transferred to this school under our father’s orders to experience a normal life.

00:21:04.980 --> 00:21:09.580
Umm, we’ll definitely return your act of kindness!

00:21:09.580 --> 00:21:11.670
Oh, you don’t have to worry about it.

00:21:12.870 --> 00:21:15.830
The fact that we met again here
must be fate!

00:21:15.830 --> 00:21:17.790
It must be fate for sure!

00:21:17.790 --> 00:21:18.790
Fate?

00:21:19.280 --> 00:21:20.750
So…

00:21:20.750 --> 00:21:24.300
…you know the Ichijou AND the Sakurazuki twins.

00:21:52.000 --> 00:21:58.000
dokomademo tsuzuku sora

00:21:52.000 --> 00:21:58.000
Oh, the sky that continues no matter where you go…

00:21:58.000 --> 00:22:04.050
daisuki na kono machi de

00:21:58.000 --> 00:22:04.050
In this town that I love…

00:22:04.050 --> 00:22:10.010
takusan no omoide to, hora,

00:22:04.050 --> 00:22:10.010
With all our memories, now look!

00:22:10.010 --> 00:22:16.020
onaji dake hohoende

00:22:10.010 --> 00:22:16.020
We are smiling the same way

00:22:16.020 --> 00:22:26.700
itsudemo kimi no tonari ni iyoutoshiteru no wa

00:22:16.020 --> 00:22:26.700
To always be trying to be besides you…

00:22:26.700 --> 00:22:39.020
mukashi kara no kuse datte omotteru kedo

00:22:26.700 --> 00:22:39.020
…is, I believe, a bad habit I’ve had for a long time

00:22:39.020 --> 00:22:45.140
“mata ashita” tte te wo furu toki ni wa

00:22:39.020 --> 00:22:45.140
When we wave our hands saying “see you tomorrow,”

00:22:45.140 --> 00:22:50.930
sukoshi dake samishii kigasuru yo

00:22:45.140 --> 00:22:50.930
I realize that I’m feeling a little lonely at that moment

00:22:50.930 --> 00:22:57.230
tooku naru kimi no senaka mitsumete

00:22:50.930 --> 00:22:57.230
Staring at your back that is getting further away,

00:22:57.230 --> 00:23:03.190
nandaka, fushigi na kimochi

00:22:57.230 --> 00:23:03.190
For some reason, a mysterious feeling…

00:23:03.190 --> 00:23:09.090
kono mune ni hirogatte yuku

00:23:03.190 --> 00:23:09.090
…is spreading through this heart of mine

00:23:11.700 --> 00:23:12.910
I’m Billy.

00:23:12.910 --> 00:23:16.250
That no-good rascal called Nozomu has run into trouble at the department store.

00:23:16.250 --> 00:23:18.960
He deserves what’s coming to him.

00:23:21.290 --> 00:23:23.670
“The Ice Cream From My Memories.”
